    "adverseDevelopmentEvidence": [
        "Initial adapter test failed because a deferred fake transport resolved only one atomic request of a multi-action nomination turn. The fixture now resolves subsequent requests and verifies no duplicate inference/commit; failed log retained.",
        "Initial clone rejected France map.setupDeck, an engine-only function omitted by the platform JSON boundary. Object helpers are now normalized identically; nonfinite numbers and non-JSON array entries remain rejected.",
        "A bounded serialization investigation traversed fresh teacher-only engineering games; no winner statistics, training labels or independent strength observations were collected or pooled.",
        "Checked-hash Python cache validation under --check-hash-based-pycs never was incomplete; authentication and a regression now cover that flag.",
        "Timeout cleanup could throw or return a rejected promise; deadline settlement now precedes contained best-effort cleanup, with regressions.",
        "Node timer truncation could expire a fractional deadline early; both transport and adapter now check the monotonic deadline and reschedule early wakes.",
        "Offline helper callers could mutate loaded weights before export or provide unvalidated fixture rows; original model fingerprints and direct fixture validation now reject these cases.",
        "Development and final latency observations differ under different host load/cache conditions. Neither is a target-host performance qualification."
    ],
